Subsoil
=======

Stratum is an independent implementation that follows the evidence-chain format
and CLI conventions of Subsoil:

  https://github.com/subsll/subsoil
  Copyright (c) 2026 Subsoil contributors
  MIT License

Subsoil is low-observable DNS reconnaissance with a SHA-256 hash-chained
evidence log. Stratum applies the same chain primitive to case files and chain
of custody. The record field order and canonical JSON rules are deliberately
compatible so Subsoil's verifier can check a Stratum ledger structurally.

Stratum contains no third-party libraries and no copied Subsoil source; the
similarities are the public evidence format and the single-binary design.
